@inject ApiMetadata Api

@* NavMenu's Overview, written by hand after the selection Overviews: organizing a sidebar, the
   current page (code), badges and counts, a row of links, and the landmark around it. Parts,
   Accessibility and See also come from the metadata and the doc comments. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>A NavMenu is a list of links that marks the link to the current page. The server works out the current page from the URL, so the menu works the same on static and interactive pages, and with <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">JavaScript off</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Organizing a sidebar</Heading>
<TextBlock>A sidebar's links can be organized into sections. To name a section, add a <Code>NavLabel</Code>. To fold some links away, put them in a <Code>NavGroup</Code>. For a line between sections, add a <Code>NavDivider</Code>. To show a count or a label on an item, set its <Code>Badge</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="nav-menu-sidebar" />
<TextBlock>A group is a native <Code>details</Code> element, so it opens and closes with JavaScript off. To start a group open, set <Code>Open</Code>. To open it on the pages at or below a path, such as <Code>/projects</Code>, set <Code>ActivePrefix</Code>. With IzzyBlazor's script, a group that contains the current page also opens itself.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">The current page</Heading>
<TextBlock>By default, an item is current on its own page and the pages below it. To make an item current on its own page only, set <Code>Match="NavLinkMatch.All"</Code>.</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Current</Code>
<List Gap="2">
    <ListItem>A link to the app's root (<Code>/</Code>) is current only on the home page.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>A link with a query string is current only when the URL has the same query.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>When several links go to one page and differ only by their query, one is current at a time. The link without a query stops being current when a link with a query matches.</ListItem>
</List>

<Heading Level="2">Badges and counts</Heading>
<TextBlock>For quiet totals with no fill, as docs and mail sidebars show them, set <Code>BadgeVariant.Plain</Code>. To give a badge a color of its own, such as <Code>Accent.Primary</Code> for an unread count, set <Code>BadgeAccent</Code>. For a status's color, set <Code>BadgeStatus</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="nav-menu-counts" />
<TextBlock>Long labels wrap rather than being cut off.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">A row of links</Heading>
<TextBlock>A horizontal nav menu is a row of section links, such as a project's pages. Set <Code>Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal"</Code>. When the links don't fit, as on a phone, the row scrolls sideways.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="nav-menu-horizontal" />
<TextBlock>For a site's main links in the header, which fold into a menu on phones, use a <Anchor Href="docs/components/site-nav">SiteNav</Anchor>. It uses the same <Code>NavItem</Code>s.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">In a landmark</Heading>
<TextBlock>A nav menu is a list, not a landmark. Put it in an <Anchor Href="docs/components/app-sidebar">AppSidebar</Anchor>, which is a <Code>nav</Code> named "Main", or in a <Code>nav</Code> element with its own <Code>aria-label</Code>.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>To show an item only on some screens, set <Code>HiddenFrom</Code> or <Code>VisibleFrom</Code> on it. They hide the whole list item.</TextBlock>

@if (OverviewParts.Of(Component, Api).Count > 0)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Parts</Heading>
}
<OverviewParts Component="Component" />

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        <AppSidebar>
            <NavMenu>
                <NavItem Href="/" Icon="Lucide.House">Home</NavItem>
                <NavItem Href="/projects" Icon="Lucide.Folder">Projects</NavItem>
                <NavItem Href="/inbox" Icon="Lucide.Inbox" Badge="4">Inbox</NavItem>
                <NavDivider />
                <NavItem Href="/settings" Icon="Lucide.Settings">Settings</NavItem>
            </NavMenu>
        </AppSidebar>
        """;

    private const string Current = """
        @* Current on /projects and on /projects/42 *@
        <NavItem Href="/projects">Projects</NavItem>

        @* Current on /reports only *@
        <NavItem Href="/reports" Match="NavLinkMatch.All">Reports</NavItem>

        @* Current on /inbox, unless Starred is *@
        <NavItem Href="/inbox">Inbox</NavItem>
        @* Current on /inbox?view=starred *@
        <NavItem Href="/inbox?view=starred">Starred</NavItem>
        """;
}
